extends ../layout/page.pug

block title
  | Discord attribution — download UI mockups · lilnas

//-
  Plan 017 (docs/features/download/plans/017-discord-attribution-and-account-
  linking.md): tdr-bot's /download command now sends the asking Discord
  identity, apps/download stores it raw, and apps/auth's admin dashboard lets
  an admin link a snowflake to a lilnas account. Resolution happens at READ
  time in apps/download, so a linked job renders identical to a web job —
  there is no separate "linked Discord" look, only "did resolution find a
  match." Four states recur everywhere a requester or actor is drawn: `web`
  (unchanged), `linked` (resolved, indistinguishable from `web`), `discord`
  (unlinked — raw username, "via Discord"), `hidden` (masked, unchanged).

//-
  The identity cell every list/table row uses. `size` sizes the avatar only
  (via `&attributes`, exactly like `requesterCell`'s own convention) — the
  text stays a fixed `text-mono-sm` regardless of row density, so a call
  site's sizing classes never leak onto layout it doesn't own (that leak is
  what broke this page's first pass: sizing classes landed on the whole row
  instead of the avatar, collapsing it into a fixed box and overflowing
  into neighbouring cells).

  The "sent via Discord, never linked" mark is a plain muted text suffix —
  `· via Discord`, `text-ink-4` against the name's `text-ink-3` — not an
  icon. A first pass used a hand-drawn Discord-ish glyph, which read as an
  unrecognisable blob at 12–16px, and even a legible icon would only be a
  hover-only affordance via its `title` attribute: invisible at a glance,
  and completely absent on a touch device. Text is always visible and reads
  standalone.
mixin discordIdentity(requester, opts)
  - opts = opts || {}
  case requester.kind
    when 'hidden'
      span(class='flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1.5')
        +avatar('–', { hidden: true, size: opts.size })&attributes(attributes)
        if !opts.nameless
          span(class='font-mono text-mono-sm text-ink-4') hidden
    when 'discord'
      span(class='flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1.5')
        +avatar(requester.initials, { size: opts.size })&attributes(attributes)
        if !opts.nameless
          span(class='truncate font-mono text-mono-sm')
            span(class='text-ink-3')= requester.username
            span(class='text-ink-4') ' · via Discord'
    default
      //- 'web' and 'linked' share one branch on purpose — a linked Discord
      //- job is resolved to the same JobRequester shape a web job carries,
      //- and rendering them identically is the feature, not an oversight.
      span(class='flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1.5')
        +avatar(requester.initials, { href: 'profile.html', size: opts.size })&attributes(attributes)
        if !opts.nameless
          a(class='truncate font-mono text-mono-sm text-ink-3 hover:text-ink hover:underline' href='profile.html')= requester.email

//- The audit-log actor cell. `service` is untouched — its own chip, never
    confused with a masked person (there is no masking on this page at all).
mixin auditActor(actor)
  if actor.kind === 'service'
    span(class='inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-mono-sm text-ink-3')
      +icon('layers')(class='h-3 w-3 text-ink-4')
      | service
  else
    +discordIdentity(actor)

mixin rowStatus(row, label)
  +chip({ label: row.live ? null : label || row.state, tone: row.tone })&attributes(attributes)
    if row.live
      +dot('live')
      = label || row.state

mixin rowArt(row)
  +poster({ shape: 'tall', v: row.v, src: row.art, radius: 'rounded-xs' })(class='w-[34px]')
    if row.icon === 'play'
      +icon('play')(class='relative z-1 h-[14px] w-[14px] text-ink-3')

block content
  -
    const STATE_LABELS = {
      web: 'Web-attributed',
      linked: 'Linked Discord (resolved)',
      discord: 'Unlinked Discord',
      hidden: 'Masked',
    }

  +mockHead({ eyebrow: 'lilnas · download', title: 'Discord attribution' })
    p(class='max-w-[62ch] text-sm text-ink-3')
      | Every download job now carries a Discord identity when it came from tdr-bot's #[+code('/download')] command.
      | An admin-linked snowflake resolves to the same lilnas identity a web job carries — indistinguishable from
      | it, everywhere — so unification is invisible when it works. An unlinked one shows the raw Discord username
      | with a small "via Discord" mark instead. Four states recur below: web, linked Discord, unlinked Discord,
      | and masked.

  //- ── activity table row set ──────────────────────────────────────────
  +appendixRule('Activity table — one row per state', 'activity')
  div(class='vp-scope')
    +viewportToggle('viewport')(class='mb-8' role='radiogroup' aria-label='Viewport')

    +viewportPanel('desktop')
      +appFrame('desktop')
        +navBar('desktop', { placeholder: 'Search or paste a link…' })
        +appBody('desktop')
          div(class='mx-auto max-w-[1080px]')
            p(class='mb-5 text-[22px] leading-[1.25] font-[650] tracking-[-0.015em]') Downloads activity
            +card()(class='px-1.5 pt-1 pb-1.5')
              +dataTable
                thead
                  tr
                    th(class='w-[38%]') item
                    th type
                    th requester
                    th status
                    th progress
                    th(class='text-right!') started
                tbody(class='stagger')
                  each row in ACTIVITY_ROWS
                    tr
                      td
                        div(class='flex items-center gap-2.5')
                          +rowArt(row)
                          span(class='text-sm')= row.title
                      td
                        +mchip(row.icon, row.kind)(class='font-mono text-mono-sm text-ink-3')
                      td
                        +discordIdentity(row.requester)(class='h-[22px] w-[22px] text-[9px]')
                      td
                        +rowStatus(row)
                      td
                        if row.progress
                          div(class='flex w-[140px] items-center gap-2')
                            +bar(row.progress)(class='flex-1')
                            span(
                              class=['font-mono text-mono-sm tabular-nums', row.quietProgress ? 'text-ink-3' : 'text-uv-hi']
                            )= `${row.progress}%`
                        else
                          span(class='font-mono text-mono-sm text-ink-4') —
                      td(class='text-right! font-mono text-mono-sm tabular-nums text-ink-3')= row.started

    +viewportPanel('mobile')
      +appFrame('mobile')
        +appBar('mobile')
          +doorplate('Download')(href='https://lilnas.io')
          span(class='flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1.5')
            +chip({ tone: 'ok' })
              +dot('live')
              | 2
            +btn({ variant: 'ghost', icon: 'search' })(class='h-[30px] w-[30px] p-0' aria-label='Search')
            +accountLink('JA')
        +appBody('mobile')
          p(class='mb-4 text-[20px] leading-[1.25] font-[650] tracking-[-0.015em]') Downloads activity
          +card()(class='px-3 py-1')
            div(class='flex flex-col stagger')
              each row in ACTIVITY_ROWS
                div(class!='flex items-center gap-3 py-[13px] [&+&]:border-t [&+&]:border-line-soft')
                  +rowArt(row)
                  div(class='flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-[7px]')
                    span(class='flex items-center justify-between gap-2')
                      span(class='flex-1 truncate text-sm')= row.short || row.title
                      span(class='shrink-0 font-mono text-mono-sm tabular-nums text-ink-4')= row.started
                    span(class='flex items-center justify-between gap-2')
                      +discordIdentity(row.requester, { size: 'xs' })(class='h-[18px] w-[18px] text-[8px]')
                      +rowStatus(row, row.mobileState || (row.live ? `${row.progress}%` : row.state))(class='h-5 shrink-0')

  p(class='mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2')
    each row in ACTIVITY_ROWS
      +chip({ label: STATE_LABELS[row.requester.kind], tone: 'mute' })

  //- ── detail-page header ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  +appendixRule('Detail-page header — attribution line', 'detail')
  div(class='mx-auto max-w-[560px]')
    +card()(class='flex flex-col gap-4 px-5 py-4')
      each row in DETAIL_HEADERS
        div(class='flex items-center justify-between gap-4 py-2 [&+&]:border-t [&+&]:border-line-soft')
          div(class='flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2')
            case row.requester.kind
              when 'hidden'
                +avatar('–', { hidden: true })(class='h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-[9px]')
                span(class='truncate font-mono text-mono-sm text-ink-4')= `hidden · ${row.when}`
              when 'discord'
                +avatar(row.requester.initials)(class='h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-[9px]')
                span(class='truncate font-mono text-mono-sm text-ink-4')= `${row.requester.username} · via Discord · ${row.when}`
              default
                +avatar(row.requester.initials, { href: 'profile.html' })(class='h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-[9px]')
                span(class='truncate font-mono text-mono-sm text-ink-4')= `downloaded by ${row.requester.email} · ${row.when}`
          span(class='shrink-0 text-right text-[12px] text-ink-3')= row.label

  //- ── admin audit-log actor cell ──────────────────────────────────────
  +appendixRule('Admin audit log — actor cell', 'audit')
  div(class='mx-auto max-w-[720px]')
    p(class='mb-[14px] text-sm text-ink-3')
      | The admin dashboard's audit log never masks — a #[+code('null')] actor there means #[strong service]
      | (no forwarded identity at all), not a hidden person. A #[+code('service')] actor keeps its existing
      | chip #[strong unchanged]; only actors carrying a Discord identity get the new treatment.
    +card({ sunk: true })(class='px-2.5 py-1')
      div(class='flex flex-col stagger')
        each line in AUDIT_ACTORS
          div(
            class='flex items-center gap-3 rounded-xs px-2.5 py-[9px] font-mono text-mono-sm transition-colors duration-[120ms] ease-uv hover:bg-surface-2'
          )
            span(class=['w-[72px] shrink-0 text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[0.08em]', line.tone])= line.level
            //-
              The actor's own width varies by state (a bare `service` chip vs.
              an avatar+email vs. an avatar+username+mark), so this is a flex
              item sized to its content rather than a fixed grid column —
              the fixed-width column this replaced is what clipped a longer
              actor into the "what" text next to it.
            span(class='shrink-0')
              +auditActor(line.actor)
            span(class='min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-ink-3')= line.what

  //- ── gallery / recent card (optional, droppable per plan E4) ─────────
  +appendixRule('Gallery card — unlinked Discord last-requester (optional, E4)', 'gallery')
  div(class='mx-auto w-[158px]')
    - const entry = GALLERY_CARD
    +gcard()(class='flex flex-col')
      +gcardLink(entry.href)
        +poster({ shape: 'tall', v: entry.v, src: entry.art, play: entry.video })
        +gcardRow
          +gcardTitle(entry.title)(class='min-h-[2.7em] flex-1')
        +gcardRow
          +mchip(entry.icon, `${entry.kind} · ${entry.meta}`)(class='font-mono text-mono-sm text-ink-3')
      +gcardRow()(class='mt-auto')
        +gcardAttrib
          +discordIdentity(entry.requester, { nameless: true })
          span(class='font-mono text-mono-sm text-ink-4')= `${entry.when} · via Discord`
